     "ruleId": "review.fp8-clamp-assumes-saturation",
     "level": "note",
     "message": {
      "text": "crates/aprender-contracts-staging/lean/Challenge/fp8-interchange-v1.lean states clampMag_le / range_e4m3 (|decode| <= E4M3_MAX) as `:= sorry` theorems. The CUDA Math API says under __NV_NOSAT an E4M3 overflow becomes NaN, not a value <= max, so the stated range holds only for a saturating (SATFINITE) conversion model. Nothing is asserted yet (all sorry); matters when someone discharges them."
     },
     "properties": {
      "grounding": "cited",
      "source": "CUDA Math API, FP8 section 3.11.1, enum __nv_saturation_t (__NV_NOSAT) via mcp__nvidia-cuda-docs__search_cuda_docs",
      "excerpt": "NOTE: for the target `fp8` types of `e4m3` and `ue5m3` kinds, the results that are larger than the maximum representable finite number of the target format become NaN.",
      "excerpt_sha256": "c624bfa1b4fb1c7f7ade327064355505826589c932cdf281c275c7d6b0ac451c",
      "failure_scenario": "A discharged range_e4m3 proof certifies a clamp that NOSAT hardware conversion does not perform; a downstream kernel contract inherits a wrong bound.",
      "precision_class": "advisory",
      "carried_forward_from": "32fc88e6f55e62edc1dfda70ddfd805a8cafaa36"
     }
